<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>
    <RootNamespace>StrangeSharpTerm.App.Tests</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.v3" />
    <PackageReference Include="Shouldly" />
    <PackageReference Include="SSH.NET" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../../src/StrangeSharpTerm.App/StrangeSharpTerm.App.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    These tests build real Avalonia objects: a Border standing in for a pane, a
    view model that is an AvaloniaObject, a control built from its XAML. Avalonia's
    property store and its weak-event bookkeeping are not written to be touched
    from several threads at once, so run in parallel the test classes take turns
    corrupting a shared pool, surfacing as "Stack empty" out of
    AvaloniaPropertyDictionaryPool, or a NullReferenceException inside
    WeakHashList, on whichever test happened to be running rather than on the one
    at fault.

    It cost five red CI runs across four different tests before it was worth
    naming. The window tests already serialise themselves for this reason; this
    assembly runs in about three seconds, so doing the same costs nothing worth
    measuring.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Content Include="xunit.runner.json" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
